{
  "challenges": [
    {
      "publicId": "chal_coding_fwp_182",
      "name": "performance-budgets",
      "type": "mini_coding",
      "title": "Fail the build on a performance budget",
      "description": "Rice Rocket's Lighthouse CI job collected three runs per page on every pull request, but nothing failed: a 600 KB analytics bundle and a hero image without dimensions both reached production. The editor holds `scripts/check-budgets.js` with its blocks missing, each marked by a `// [ ]` line; some pieces are wrong on purpose. Fill every line so that: each metric is judged on the median of the runs, so one noisy run neither fails nor passes a page on its own; a budget applies to the pages its pattern names (`*` stands for exactly one path segment); a budget at level `error` fails the build and one at level `warn` only warns; a metric listed under `regression` fails the build when it grew more than that fraction since main, even under its budget, and a page that is new on this branch has no baseline to compare with; errors come before warnings, each group sorted. Run checks reports built from real-looking runs.",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "outcomes": [
        "fast-loading"
      ],
      "points": 40,
      "hints": [
        "Go through one page at a time: which budgets name it, what single value represents its three runs, and what does main's report say about the same metric?",
        "Look at how a median differs from a mean on [2200, 2100, 5900], how a pattern with `*` becomes a regular expression anchored at both ends, and at growth as `(now - before) / before`.",
        "A bundle-size check on another project: `const size = median(runs.map((r) => r.cssKB)); if (size > budget.max) lines.push(...)`, with `matchesPath(\"/blog/*\", \"/blog/2026/post\")` false because `*` must not cross a `/`."
      ],
      "coding": {
        "language": "javascript",
        "filePath": "scripts/check-budgets.js",
        "executionMode": "browser",
        "timeLimitMs": 2000,
        "memoryLimitMb": 128,
        "scoringMode": "all_or_nothing",
        "maxAttempts": null
      },
